---
import PageLayout from '../../layouts/PageLayout.astro';
import ContentTable from '../../components/ContentTable.astro';
import Sources from '../../components/Sources.astro';
import { YEAR } from '../../data/site-config';
import { route } from '../../i18n/routes';
import { breadcrumbSchema, webPageSchema } from '../../lib/seo';
import { taux, MV, ASF, MODES, P } from '../../lib/engine/pension';
import { formatMoney, formatPercent, formatDecimal } from '../../lib/format';
const lang = 'en';
const $ = (x: number) => formatMoney(x, 0, lang);

const title = 'Child support France: calculation method and sources';
const description = 'How this French child support calculator works: the Ministry of Justice formula, 2026 parameters and sources, automated tests, and what it does not do.';
---
<PageLayout title={title} description={description} lang={lang} jsonLd={[webPageSchema({ name: 'Methodology and sources of the French child support calculator', description, path: route('method', lang), lang }), breadcrumbSchema([{ name: 'Home', path: route('home', lang) }, { name: 'Methodology', path: route('method', lang) }])]} breadcrumbs={[{ label: 'Methodology' }]}>
  <header class="mb-6"><h1 class="text-3xl font-bold text-navy-900 md:text-4xl">Methodology and sources of the French child support calculator</h1><p class="mt-3 text-lg text-navy-600">Every figure on this site can be redone by hand: here are the formula, the parameters, their sources and the limits.</p></header>
  <div class="prose prose-slate max-w-none">
    <h2>The formula</h2>
    <p>The calculator reproduces the reference table published by the French Ministry of Justice on justice.fr:</p>
    <p><strong>support per child = (paying parent’s net taxable monthly income − subsistence amount) × rate per child</strong>, then <strong>total support = support per child × number of children</strong>.</p>
    <p>The subsistence amount is the table’s {$(MV)}, matching the single-person RSA flat rate ({formatMoney(P.rsa.personne_seule, 2, lang)} from 1 April {YEAR}). The rate per child depends on the number of children (1 to 6) and on visiting time (reduced, standard, shared). Income at or below the subsistence amount gives zero support. Beyond six children the official table stops; the engine then uses the six-child rate, a calculation convention flagged as such.</p>
    <ContentTable caption="Reference table rates per child" headers={['Children', 'Reduced', 'Standard', 'Shared']} align={['l', 'r', 'r', 'r']} rows={[1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6].map((n) => [String(n), ...MODES.map((m) => formatPercent(taux(n, m), 1, lang))])} />
    <h2>Other calculations</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>ASF</strong>: {formatMoney(ASF, 2, lang)} per child; top-up ASF = ASF − support per child, nothing if the gap is below €{P.asf.seuil_non_versement} (service-public.fr, sheet F815).</li>
      <li><strong>Indexation</strong>: amount × new index ÷ base index (sheet F2010), tested on the official example €300 → €344.65.</li>
      <li><strong>Arrears</strong>: {P.recouvrement.anciennete_max_ans} years recoverable; direct payment covers {P.recouvrement.paiement_direct_mois_arrieres} months of arrears spread over {P.recouvrement.paiement_direct_etalement_mois} months (sheets F1249, F998).</li>
      <li><strong>Tax</strong>: progressive scale for {P.fiscalite.revenus} income and the number of shares entered, without décote or family-quotient cap; uncapped deduction for a minor child, {$(P.fiscalite.plafond_majeur)} per adult child; 10% allowance on support received, minimum {$(P.fiscalite.abattement_min_par_pensionne)}, maximum {$(P.fiscalite.abattement_max_par_foyer)} (sheets F2, F35777, F1419).</li>
    </ul>
    <h2>Automated tests</h2>
    <p>Four full rows of the official table (€700, €1,500, €2,000 and €2,300, 72 amounts) are compared with justice.fr to the cent on every build, together with service-public.fr’s worked examples (indexation, income tax scale, compensatory payment reduction). Any gap blocks publication.</p>
    <h2>Parameters and sources</h2>
    <ContentTable headers={['Parameter', 'Value', 'Source']} align={['l', 'r', 'l']} rows={[
      ['Table subsistence amount', $(MV), 'justice.fr, scale'],
      ['RSA, single person', formatMoney(P.rsa.personne_seule, 2, lang), 'service-public.fr F19778'],
      ['ASF per child (1 April 2026)', formatMoney(ASF, 2, lang), 'service-public.fr F815'],
      ['Deduction cap, adult child', $(P.fiscalite.plafond_majeur), 'service-public.fr F2'],
      ['Flat housing allowance, adult child', $(P.fiscalite.forfait_hebergement_majeur), 'service-public.fr F2'],
      ['INSEE index Nov 2025, all households', formatDecimal(P.revalorisation.indice_ensemble_nov_2025, 2, lang), 'service-public.fr F2010'],
      ['INSEE index Nov 2025, urban households', formatDecimal(P.revalorisation.indice_urbains_nov_2025, 2, lang), 'service-public.fr F2010'],
    ]} />
    <p>Parameters live in a single dated file ({P.retrieved_at}); no value is hard-coded in the pages.</p>
    <h2>What the tool does not do</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>It does not replace the judge: the table is guidance, and the judge weighs the child’s needs and each parent’s costs.</li>
      <li>It ignores the receiving parent’s income, as the table does.</li>
      <li>It handles several families only by showing two readings of the table.</li>
      <li>Tax is an estimate: no décote, no family-quotient cap, no tax reductions or credits.</li>
      <li>ASF conditions (living alone, dependent child) are assumed when you tick “lives alone”.</li>
    </ul>
    <Sources lang="en" />
  </div>
</PageLayout>
